<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sappi strike still on, supply not disrupted.</title>
<headline>Sappi strike still on, supply not disrupted.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African paper and pulp producer Sappi Ltd said a strike at its Adamas mill continued on Friday but production was running normally despite the action.</p>
<p>&quot;The situation was peaceful, both machines continued to run and supplies to customers were not disrupted,&quot; the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said last Friday that the No.3 machine would be shut down over the weekend and started up again on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
